course: dictionary
lesson: 1994
title: What is a computer?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A computer is a machine that stores information and follows instructions. It helps us write, count, draw, play games, send messages and look things up. Laptops, tablets and even phones are all kinds of computers.
explain: Computers are very fast, but they only do what their programs tell them. «A computer does not feel, want or know anything; it only follows its programs.» When a computer seems clever, the thinking was really done earlier by the people who wrote the instructions.
explain: Computers are used in many places. «A factory robot is controlled by a computer that drives motors in each joint.» At school you can use computers for typing, coding and computing lessons.
fact: A computer is a machine that stores information and follows instructions.
fact: Laptops, tablets and phones are kinds of computers.
fact: «A computer does not feel, want or know anything.»
fact: «AI means artificial intelligence: computer programs that do tasks like talking, sorting or answering.»
fact: «A girl in Ohio downloaded a cheat for an online game from a site that promised free gems; it put a virus on the family computer.» Keep your passwords secret, and tell an adult if something online upsets you.
exercise: What is a computer? | *A machine that stores information and follows instructions | A kind of food | A book with pictures of animals | A plant that grows in the ground
exercise: «A computer does not feel, want or know anything.» What does this tell us? | *A computer only follows the programs people wrote for it | Computers have feelings like people | Computers know everything | Computers can decide for themselves what they want to do
exercise: Which of these is a kind of computer? | Pencil case | Football | *Tablet | Bicycle
test: «AI means artificial intelligence: computer programs that do tasks like talking, sorting or answering.» What does AI mean? | A computer that has feelings | *Computer programs that do tasks like talking or sorting | A type of animal | A kind of game
test: Which is the safest thing to do online? | *Tell an adult if something online upsets you | Share your password with a friend | Click every link that promises free gems | Give your password to anyone who asks
exam: Ella says her computer feels sad when it is switched off. Is she right? | Yes, but only at night | *No, a computer does not feel anything; it only follows its programs | Sometimes, if the computer is very old | Yes, it feels sad because it is lonely
